<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN" "task.dtd">
<task id="AddingPointsWithOPCUAHistoriesOpcUA-550DEB3F" xml:lang="en-us" class="- topic/topic task/task "><title class="- topic/title ">Adding points containing OPC UA histories</title><shortdesc class="- topic/shortdesc ">If the OPC UA point you are adding has an OPC UA history,
the point automatically includes a history extension (<uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">ImportHistoryExt</uicontrol>).</shortdesc><prolog class="- topic/prolog "><metadata class="- topic/metadata "><keywords class="- topic/keywords "><indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">points<indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">adding histories</indexterm></indexterm><indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">histories<indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">adding points with histories</indexterm></indexterm></keywords></metadata></prolog><taskbody class="- topic/body task/taskbody "><prereq class="- topic/section task/prereq ">Discovered objects with histories are visible in the <wintitle class="+ topic/keyword ui-d/wintitle ">Opc Ua Client Point Manager</wintitle> view.</prereq><context class="- topic/section task/context "/><steps class="- topic/ol task/steps "><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">To open the <wintitle class="+ topic/keyword ui-d/wintitle ">Opc Ua Client Point Manager</wintitle>, expand <menucascade class="+ topic/ph ui-d/menucascade "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Config</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Drivers</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">OpcUaNetwork</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">OpcUaDevice</uicontrol></menucascade> and double-click the <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Points</uicontrol> folder.</cmd></step><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">To run a discovery job, click <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Discover</uicontrol>.</cmd></step><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">To confirm that the points have histories, examine them
in the <wintitle class="+ topic/keyword ui-d/wintitle ">Opc Ua Client Point Manager</wintitle>.</cmd><stepresult class="- topic/itemgroup task/stepresult "><image placement="break" scale="60" href="../graphic/opcuaObjectsWithHistories_0000026080.png" class="- topic/image "/>Here are two ways to identify
OPC UA objects that have histories:<ul class="- topic/ul "><li class="- topic/li "><p class="- topic/p ">A triangular history badge appears over the icon of the OPC
UA object in the <wintitle class="+ topic/keyword ui-d/wintitle ">Discovered</wintitle> pane, for example: <image href="../graphic/HistoryBadge_0000024077.png" class="- topic/image "/></p></li><li class="- topic/li "><p class="- topic/p ">The value under the Historizing column in the <wintitle class="+ topic/keyword ui-d/wintitle ">Discovered</wintitle> pane reports <systemoutput class="+ topic/ph sw-d/systemoutput ">true</systemoutput>.</p></li></ul></stepresult></step><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">Select one or more objects with histories and click <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Add</uicontrol>.</cmd><info class="- topic/itemgroup task/info ">The default history extension period for uploading history data
is once in 10 minutes. To modify this period, configure the <parmname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/parmname ">Execution Time</parmname> property by changing the <parmname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/parmname ">Interval</parmname> value.</info></step><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">To view histories on the property sheet, right-click the
point and click <menucascade class="+ topic/ph ui-d/menucascade "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Views</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Property Sheet</uicontrol></menucascade>.</cmd><stepresult class="- topic/itemgroup task/stepresult "/></step></steps></taskbody></task>